    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Denmark was one of the first-settled places in Madison County, with land opened by Thomas Sanders in 1822.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1854 the town was incorporated, but the Tennessee General Assembly later revoked its charter in 1983, leaving it unincorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s economy collapsed after the Civil War because no railroads were built through it, a fate echoed in many nearby communities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Union soldiers repelled a Confederate raid near Denmark in the Battle of Britton's Lane in September 1862.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The antebellum Denmark Presbyterian Church, still standing, is one of the few remaining structures from the town’s once-thriving farming era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Big Black Creek Historical Association preserves Denmark’s heritage, promoting sites across eastern Haywood and western Madison Counties.",
